WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.633
In this walkthrough we'll see who is
allowed to approve what, and which roles
carry which permissions, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:19.600
Approval Chains shows the sign-off required before a
consequential action completes. It is read-only here —
this is the configuration, not a queue of things waiting for you.

3
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:30.933
Each chain names the thing being approved, the condition
that triggers it, and the steps in order. Publishing a
curve, for instance, requires a risk manager to approve it.

4
00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:43.167
Chains are filtered by asset class and by amount band,
because approval requirements usually step up with size. A
small trade and a large one can follow entirely different routes.

5
00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:52.700
Approval decides who signs off. What a person
may do in the first place comes from their
role, and Roles Viewer lays those out as a matrix.

6
00:00:52.700 --> 00:01:02.633
Every configured role gets a column, and every
permission a row. Reading down a column tells
you what that role can do across the whole system.

7
00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:13.433
This is the reference to reach for when someone cannot see
a screen or a button. Compare the permission they need
against the roles they hold, and the gap is usually obvious.

8
00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:21.400
That completes Approvals and Roles. Every surface
shown here can also be opened from the agent
panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
